    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good high-level summary, but my evaluators need something more granular to actually use during interviews. We're talking about high-stakes board meetings and global leadership. \n\nCan you get more specific about the physical and verbal cues? Like, what does this \"commanding authority\" actually look like in practice? Think about things like vocal tone, body language, how they carry themselves in a room, and even their general aesthetic or mannerisms. I need to be able to tell them exactly what a \"high-potential\" candidate looks and sounds like compared to someone who just seems like a middle manager.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
