      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In physical presentation, commanding authority often manifests as deliberate, controlled movement and impeccable, understated grooming, conveying polish without being flashy. Verbally, an executive will use a measured pace with varied cadence, projecting warmth through vocal tone while ensuring their diction is precise and impactful. Body language involves taking up space confidently—a grounded stance, purposeful gestures, and maintaining engaged eye contact across the room. These cues collectively signal preparedness and the conviction that they are equipped to lead at the highest levels.",
      "source": "target",
